course: dictionary
lesson: 125
title: Advance: forward and ahead
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Advance is a useful word with a few meanings, and the clues in the sentence tell you which one. It can mean to move forward, as in «The army advanced across the field.» It can also mean to improve or make progress: «Science has advanced a lot.»
explain: The most common phrase is «in advance», which means before something happens. In «Book in advance», the words tell you to book before the day. «Let the coach know in advance if you will miss practice» means tell them before, not on the day.
explain: Try the swap test: put "before" or "forward" into the sentence. If it still makes sense, you have found the right meaning. An advance can also be a noun, like «advances in medicine», meaning new improvements.
fact: To advance means to move forward or to make progress.
fact: «In advance» means before something happens.
fact: An advance can be a forward movement, or an improvement, such as «advances in medicine».
fact: As an adjective, advance means done or given early, as in «advance warning».
fact: In «The sender paid a penny in advance, whatever the distance», the money was paid before the letter was sent.
exercise: «Book your tickets in advance.» What does in advance mean here? | During the show | Only if it rains | After the show | *Before the show happens
exercise: «The army advanced slowly across the field.» What does advanced mean here? | Fell asleep | *Moved forward | Went backwards | Stopped and rested
exercise: «Science has advanced a lot in the last hundred years.» What does advanced mean here? | Broke into pieces | Got smaller | *Made progress and improved | Stayed exactly the same
test: A coach says, «Tell me in advance if you will miss practice.» What should you do? | Never tell anyone | *Tell the coach before the practice day | Tell the coach after the practice | Wait and see what happens
test: What does «advances in medicine» mean? | *New improvements and progress in medicine | Forward moves made by an army | The price of a medicine | Old, broken tools
exam: In «knowing it in advance makes asking easier», what does in advance mean? | Without telling anyone | *Before you need it | When the school bell rings | Only after a crisis
